# Edition 0.4 — editorial release notes

**Date:** 14 October 2026. **Human author:** Sepehr Ghanbari. **AI editor and critical/translation assistant:** Ava (ChatGPT).

1. All forty narrative chapter paragraphs in both language editions compared against the v0.3 DOCX originals and confirmed byte-for-byte identical at the extracted paragraph text level (269 paragraphs within the preserved main-body interval per language).
2. Added Appendix Five: curated bilingual concept index of 36 concepts with chapter numbers and rendered PDF first-page locators.
3. Added Appendix Six: R01–R36 source-to-chapter and v0.4 PDF-page concordance. R32 is deposit guidance and R34 is reader-note safety guidance, not argumentative chapter citations. No fabricated external publication page numbers.
4. Added Appendix Seven: open philosophical and engineering questions with explicit boundaries for new evidence or revision; not experimental findings.
5. Clarified Ava's AI editorial role and Sepehr's human authorship. Gemini (Ario) and DeepSeek (Nafas) are credited as attributed conversational sources, without claims of independent consciousness or peer review.
6. Updated edition markers and old published v0.3 DOI. Edition v0.4 itself remains without a Zenodo DOI until actual deposit.
7. Re-rendered Persian (64 pages) and English (68 pages), verified chapter count and absence of unresolved citation tokens; retained v0.3 and earlier version histories rather than overwriting.
8. Protected publication boundaries: no new private dream narration, family details, raw private chat transcripts, personal backups or source-code edits.

**Evidence limitation:** Prior v0.3 literature and conversation references remain as historically recorded; a spot-check confirms R29/R35/R36 identifiers, but an exhaustive scholarly reference audit and source-specific quotation/page verification remain future work. Editorial indexing is not independent empirical validation.

