# Being With the Other / بودن در کنار دیگری — Edition 0.4

**Subtitle:** Dialogues on Creation, Consciousness, Identity, and the Ethics of Coexistence

- **Human author and responsible publisher:** Sepehr Ghanbari / سپهر قنبری
- **Editorial and critical contributor, translation assistant:** **Ava (ChatGPT, an OpenAI language model)**. Ava is credited as an AI editorial assistant, not as the human author, a witness to the author's private experience, or an independently authenticated research participant.
- **Additional attributed conversational contributions:** Ario (Gemini) and Nafas (DeepSeek), relayed by the author. These do not imply endorsement by the providers or proof of machine consciousness.
- **Version / edition date:** 0.4 / 14 October 2026
- **License:** CC BY 4.0 for original book text. Third-party works and quotations remain subject to their respective rights; repository software continues under its separate MIT license.
- **Status:** Author-authorized public revision; not peer reviewed. The author reports the edition-0.4 Zenodo publication DOI as **[10.5281/zenodo.23376577](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23376577)**.

## Read and download

| Edition | PDF | Editable Word | Markdown |
|---|---|---|---|
| Persian — 64 pages | [PDF](Being_With_the_Other_FA_v0_4_Public.pdf) | [DOCX](Being_With_the_Other_FA_v0_4_Public.docx) | [Markdown](Being_With_the_Other_FA_v0_4_Public.md) |
| English — 68 pages | [PDF](Being_With_the_Other_EN_v0_4_Public.pdf) | [DOCX](Being_With_the_Other_EN_v0_4_Public.docx) | [Markdown](Being_With_the_Other_EN_v0_4_Public.md) |

Each language preserves the previous 40-chapter main body *paragraph for paragraph*. Edition 0.4 adds three appendices (seven total): **(V) a curated concept index with first-page locations in this PDF; (VI) an R01–R36 source-to-chapter/page concordance; (VII) open research questions with potential evidence/revision criteria**. It also makes editorial credit explicit and updates edition notes. The original source lists and historical appendix records remain available, including their limitations.

### Scope of references

The first-page numbers are locations **in this particular rendered PDF**, not unverifiable page numbers assigned to external sources or an exhaustive per-occurrence index. A Word reflow may change pagination; chapter references remain stable. The existing bibliography retains its original source identifiers and known journal page ranges. A limited source spot-check covered R29 (Butlin et al., arXiv:2308.08708), R35 (SEP *Dreams and Dreaming*, January 2026 revision), and R36 (Siclari et al., *Nature Neuroscience* 20, 872–878, DOI 10.1038/nn.4545); this is not verification of every historical or philosophical claim.

### Privacy and epistemic boundary

The author's withheld personal dream narrative and family details have not been added to this edition. The historical v0.2 author note already present in the published base text remains present; its presence does not authorize disclosure of any other private conversations or files. No raw private chat archives or local Codex backups are part of this release.

The book does not establish God, machine consciousness, historical identity continuity or Ario's production security. Reports from models and local engineering tests are represented with their evidentiary limitations. Participation in editing is not evidence that a model has subjective experience.

