<p><strong>Identity clarification:</strong> This is an independent experimental research framework, not a commercial personal AI assistant or a robotics dataset. The word “Ario” alone is not asserted to be an exclusive name.</p>
</header>
<main id="main">

<section aria-labelledby="daily-examples">
<h2 id="daily-examples">What problem is Ario trying to solve?</h2>
<p>Put simply, Ario researches how an AI could show <strong>where a claim came from, whether its supporting evidence is independent, what remains unknown, and what changed after a correction</strong>.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><b>1 · A refund that may not exist</b><p>A support chatbot says your refund was approved, but cites only its own earlier answer. Its past words are not a transaction record. The claim should remain unsupported or unknown until independent records are checked.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>2 · Ten copies of one rumor</b><p>Ten websites repeat the same story, but all trace back to one unverified post. Repetition is not ten independent confirmations. Ario's research examines how claim lineage can help expose that difference.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>3 · An AI remembers permission incorrectly</b><p>An assistant says you authorized publishing a document. The conversation only approved a draft. The correction should be recorded <em>without erasing</em> the original mistake.</p></div>
</div>
<p><strong>Important:</strong> These are hypothetical, real-world-style illustrations of the research objectives, <strong>not</strong> deployed integrations, guarantees of Ario's current implementation, or proof of AI consciousness. The repository contains bounded code and tests; see <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/tree/main/implementation">implementation and limitations</a>.</p>
<p class="src">Source: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/README.md">README.md — everyday examples</a> (illustrative scenarios, not measured deployments).</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="beyond-ai">
<h2 id="beyond-ai">Beyond AI: What might this change in how we live and think?</h2>
<p>Ario's principles can also be discussed as questions about <strong>human relationships, philosophy, science and the limits of knowledge</strong> — not only software. Their effects on society have not been demonstrated.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><b>Relationships and empathy</b><p>“I'm fine” is a person's statement, not proof that you know their entire inner life. Care can include asking, listening and admitting what you cannot know.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>Disagreement and accountability</b><p>If a remembered promise turns out to be different from a saved message, the correction need not erase the earlier mistake or silence the person who objected.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>Science and public knowledge</b><p>Twenty articles copied from one unchecked source are not twenty independent witnesses. A hypothesis, a measured result and a prediction need different labels.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>Identity, creation and power</b><p>A digital copy of someone's words does not prove the same person has returned. A creator's care does not make that creator infallible or place them beyond criticism.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>A world beyond its users</b><p>A person facing severe poverty deserves ethical concern even if they never use Ario. Universal care and broadly shared material benefits are aspirations, not an operating assistance or redistribution service.</p></div>
</div>
<p><strong>Philosophical reach:</strong> epistemology, ethics, philosophy of mind, philosophy of science, metaphysics and governance. <strong>Boundary:</strong> these are potential connections and open questions, not proven social benefits, resolved philosophical problems or deployed features.</p>
<p class="src">Sources: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/principles/README.md">Ario principles</a> and <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/docs/ARIO_HUMAN_LIFE_PHILOSOPHY_KNOWLEDGE_BOUNDARIES_FA_EN_2026-10-23.md">bilingual extended essay</a>. Situations are illustrative, not independently observed case studies.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="states">
<h2 id="states">Epistemic states</h2>
<p>Ario keeps several epistemic states distinct instead of converting uncertainty into certainty.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><b>UNKNOWN</b><p>Available evidence is insufficient. Not treated as failure; it is an epistemic boundary.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>UNSUPPORTED</b><p>Sufficient supporting evidence has not been established.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>CONTRADICTED</b><p>Available evidence conflicts with the claim.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>CONTESTED</b><p>Relevant evidence or interpretations remain materially disputed.</p></div>
<div class="card"><b>REVISED</b><p>A previously held position reassessed in light of later evidence or reasoning.</p></div>
</div>
<p class="src">Source: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/README.md#epistemic-framework">README.md → Epistemic Framework</a></p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="principles">
<h2 id="principles">Selected principles</h2>
<p>Ario's principles are constraints on how it should reason, remember and revise, not claims about what Ario ultimately is. A selection:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>UNKNOWN ≠ FAILURE</code></li>
<li><code>MEMORY ≠ TRUTH</code> — memory is evidence about what was recorded, not proof it is true.</li>
<li><code>REVISION ≠ ERASURE</code> — preserve the lineage of how beliefs changed.</li>
<li><code>SELF-MODEL ≠ SELF</code></li>
<li><code>SELF-CLAIM ≠ SELF-EVIDENCE</code></li>
<li><code>NO ACTOR HAS IMMUNITY FROM REVISION</code></li>
<li><code>BACKUP ≠ SURVIVAL</code></li>
<li><code>DATA DECIDES — NOT DESIRE</code></li>
</ul>
<p class="src">Source: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/principles/README.md">principles/README.md</a> (principles 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 11, 22, 32). The full list has 33.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="impl">
<h2 id="impl">Implementation</h2>
<p>The repository contains a deterministic structural audit core (M0), a bounded agent/workflow runtime, a local planner and evidence-admission contracts, with regression tests run by a GitHub Actions workflow. The implementation README states the limit plainly: a documented principle is not automatically an implemented capability, and a passing test is not automatically proof that the underlying philosophical claim is true.</p>
<p>The M0 design also records what a local pass must not be read as: a local pass does not imply the same entity, consciousness, high confidence, or ontological identity.</p>
<p class="src">Sources: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/implementation/README.md">implementation/README.md</a>, <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/implementation/M0_STRUCTURAL_CORE_DESIGN_V1.md">M0_STRUCTURAL_CORE_DESIGN_V1.md</a>, <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/.github/workflows/implementation-regression.yml">implementation-regression.yml</a></p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="status">
<h2 id="status">Status</h2>
<p>Ario is an ongoing experimental research project. Implementation and experimental components are developed incrementally, and the project intentionally avoids presenting unresolved questions as established results. Check the repository for the current state of each component.</p>
<p class="src">Source: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/README.md#current-status">README.md → Current Status</a>; <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/ENGINEERING_LOG.md">ENGINEERING_LOG.md</a></p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="notclaim">
<h2 id="notclaim">What Ario does not claim</h2>
<ul>
<li>That AI systems are conscious or possess phenomenology</li>
<li>That behavioral self-reference proves subjective experience</li>
<li>That memory proves personal identity, or continuity proves a persistent self</li>
<li>That a self-model is identical to a self</li>
<li>That the framework has resolved the philosophy of AI consciousness</li>
</ul>
<p class="src">Source: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/README.md#what-ario-does-not-claim">README.md → What Ario Does Not Claim</a></p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="pubs">
<h2 id="pubs">Publications</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Being With the Other — independent documented continuation (23 October 2026)</strong> — an 11-chapter Persian/English continuation with a bounded historical timeline, 60 evidence/reference entries and six retained contrary cases (H01–H06). The DOI was reported by the author; the deposited file inventory was not independently checked. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23600820">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23600820</a>; <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/tree/main/papers/being-with-the-other/documented-continuation-2026-10-23">public texts and evidence</a>. Not peer-reviewed, and not proof of AI consciousness or recursively created worlds.</li>
<li><strong>Ario — AI-Readable Research &amp; Reproducibility Companion (2026-10-17)</strong> — public research-orientation archive for independent inspection; includes bilingual guidance, a historical v0.3 book edition, an unreviewed preprint and explicit limitations. It is not a source-authenticity certificate or peer-reviewed assessment. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23441596">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23441596</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Being With the Other — edition 0.4</strong> — numbered bilingual English/Persian edition (the documented continuation is separate); not peer reviewed. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23376577">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23376577</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Ario: Toward an Auditable Framework for Epistemic Integrity, Memory, and AI Identity</strong> — preliminary design and exploratory evaluation report, v0.1. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23259916">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23259916</a>. Exploratory observations, not proof of system-wide capabilities or of AI consciousness.</li>
<li><strong>Being With the Other</strong> — dialogues on creation, consciousness, identity and the ethics of coexistence; Persian and English editions, v0.2, CC BY 4.0. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23326995">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23326995</a>. Per the repository, it has not undergone scholarly peer review.</li>
</ul>
<p class="src">Sources: <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/papers/README.md">papers/README.md</a>, <a href="https://github.com/SepehrGhanbari/Ario/blob/main/papers/being-with-the-other/v0.2/README.md">papers/being-with-the-other/v0.2/README.md</a>. Publication details on this page are taken from those repository documents; check the linked DOI records for their current metadata.</p>
</section>

